            <ArticleTitle>The third head of gastrocnemius in CT images.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 17 year old male patient was undergoing a CT scan for pain and swelling of the left knee. The CT images of both legs, taken simultaneously, revealed an asymmetry of the musculature in the popliteal fossa of the right leg. Serial images indicated the presence of a third head joining the medial head of gastrocnemius.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
